Analyzing Data frames 

viewing the data -
head()--- by default it takes first 5 rows 
head(10)--- first 10 rows 

tail() --- by default it takes last 5 rows 
tail(10) -- last 10 rows 

info() --- return all about the data 

--------------------------------------------------

cleaning the data

data cleaning 
data cleaning means fixing bad data in your data set 
bad data could be :
empty cells
Data in wrong format 
wrong data
Duplicates

A. 1. empty cells - Empty cells can potentially give you a wrong result when you analyze data.

remove rows = by remove rows --- use dropna() --- to remove the empty rows
 dropna(inplace=True) // remove all rows with NULL values 

 2. Replace Empty values 
 use fillna(130,inplace=true) // it fills the null values with 130 values 

 3. Replace using MEAN , MEDIAN , MODE 

 x = df["Calories"].mean()//median()//mode()

df.fillna({"Calories": x}, inplace=True)4

B. 1. cleaning data of Wrong format 

To fix it, you have two options: remove the rows, or convert all cells in the columns into the same format.

how to covert the data into datetime
use to_datetime()

C. 1. Fixing Wrong data 
by replacing it to right value using loc it is for the small datasets 
for the large datasets ---- create some rules , condition 
Another method is to remove the wrong data 

D. 1. Removing Duplicates 
to checkm that duplicates value present or not then use duplicated()
for removing this we use , drop_duplicates(inplace=True)

inplace=true means the method does not return a new dataframe, but it will remove all deuplicates from the original dataframe 


----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data corrrelations 
1. finding relationships - 
a great aspect of the pandas module is the corr() method

A corr() method is used to calcultes the relationship between the each columns 

the number varies from -1 to 1
1 means that there is a 1 to 1 relationship 
0.9 is also a god relationship means if you increse the one value , the other will also increase (it is the mean of the +ve correlation)
-0.9 is also good relationship as 0.9 but if we increase the value of any by 1 , other will probably decrease.
0.2 is not good relationship

What is a good correlation? It depends on the use, but I think it is safe to say you have to have at least 0.6 (or -0.6) to call it a good correlation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pandas plotting

plotting -- 
use plot() method to create diagrams 
for this we must import matplotlib.pyplot as plt to plot the diagram 

1. scatter plot- it needs x and y- axis  
specify using kind argument

e.g - import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

df = pd.read_csv('data.csv')

df.plot(kind = 'scatter', x = 'Duration', y = 'Calories')

plt.show()

2. Histogram 
use kind = hist 
a histogram needs only one column 
it shows the frequency of each interval

